Amethystora is built on Universal Blue's images (https://universal-blue.org)
and includes software from Universal Blue's projects, copyright their
contributors and licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0, among them:

  - ublue-os/main  https://github.com/ublue-os/main
  - ublue-os/brew  https://github.com/ublue-os/brew
  - ublue-os/uupd  https://github.com/ublue-os/uupd

Amethystora modifies these and renames them at build time, with the scripts in
build_files/ of https://github.com/iarsslen/amethystora. Parts of that
repository began as files of Universal Blue's projects and are modified for
Amethystora: the Containerfile, the Justfile, .github/ and build_files/, and
the desktop layer in system_files/shared.

Amethystora is built from the packages of Fedora Linux. Fedora and the Fedora
logo are trademarks of Red Hat, Inc. Amethystora is not provided, supported or
endorsed by the Fedora Project or by Red Hat; Fedora itself is at
https://fedoraproject.org/. An image carries neither Fedora's logos nor its
release packages, which Fedora's trademark guidelines ask a system built this
way to replace: the artwork is Amethystora's own, and Fedora's generic-release
stands in the package database for fedora-release.

GNOME Tour (GPL-3.0-or-later, https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/gnome-tour) is
not the app as Fedora builds it. Fedora puts a picture with Fedora's logo on
its first page; since October 2026 Amethystora replaces that picture with its
own each time an image is built (build_files/base/12-tour.sh).

fprintd (GPL-2.0-or-later, https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/libfprint/fprintd),
which reads fingerprints, is not the package as Fedora builds it either. Each
image build makes it again from Fedora's spec with seven patches, kept in
packaging/fprintd of the repository under fprintd's licence: six of fprintd's
own, from its development after its release 1.94.5, and one of Amethystora's,
the duress finger in pam_fprintd. Its source package travels in the image, in
usr/src/amethystora.

Solaar's udev rules (GPL-2.0-or-later, https://github.com/pwr-Solaar/Solaar),
/usr/lib/udev/rules.d/42-logitech-unify-permissions.rules from Fedora's
solaar-udev package, are changed when an image is built: the line that gives
/dev/uinput to whoever sits at the machine is taken out, and the file says so
(build_files/base/08-hardening.sh). Its source is Fedora's package.

