The file-watch sensor in usr/libexec/amethystora-sensor (apps/sensor/) is one
more program of the same build, which watches the files the audit rules watch
without their per-system-call cost (plans/done/PLAN-audit-cost.md). Its BPF
object is Amethystora's own code, under the GNU General Public License, version
2, or the BSD 2-Clause License at your option, so it may use the kernel's
GPL-only BPF helpers; that licence ships in usr/share/licenses/amethystora-sensor.
It wraps the kernel's libbpf through the libbpf-rs and libbpf-sys crates, under
the GNU Lesser General Public License, version 2.1, or the BSD 2-Clause License;
these and its other crates are in the list beside the apps'. It links the libbpf
the image already carries, nothing of it vendored.

The AI agent's tools in usr/libexec/amethystora-agent-tools and
usr/libexec/amethystora-agent-root (apps/agent-tools/) are two more programs of
the same build; their crates are in the same list. Their search ranks passages
by meaning with potion-base-8M, a static embedding model by MinishLab made with
Model2Vec, under the MIT License, which ships unchanged in
usr/share/amethystora/agents/knowledge/model. It is distilled from BAAI's
bge-base-en-v1.5, under the MIT License, and its vocabulary is BERT's, under the
Apache License, version 2.0; all three licences ship in
usr/share/licenses/potion-base-8M, with where the model comes from.

  - potion-base-8M     https://huggingface.co/minishlab/potion-base-8M
  - bge-base-en-v1.5   https://huggingface.co/BAAI/bge-base-en-v1.5
  - BERT               https://github.com/google-research/bert

